# Stranglethorn Vale (36-37): the first Horde quests of Grom'gol, Booty Bay and Nesingwary's
# Expedition, and the Ruins of Zul'Kunda, for a Horde duo.
#
# Built into the addon with:
#   python3 addon/tools/guide_build.py addon/guides/stranglethorn_vale_36_37.guide --db data/forever.sqlite
#
# Research (November 2026): givers, objectives, prerequisites and the places of mobs and objects
# from the game data (data/forever.sqlite), checked against outof.games (Stranglethorn Vale, area 33).
# The quest list is section 16 of addon/guides/horde_1_40_allocation.md. The later Stranglethorn
# quests (the next Mastery quests, Kin'weelay's, the ogres of Grom'gol...) are in Stranglethorn Vale
# & Swamp of Sorrows (41-43) and the guides after it.
# Carried in (skipped by those who lack them): Hemet Nesingwary (5762, from Kravel Koalbeard at the
#   Shimmering Flats, Thousand Needles), Hunting in Stranglethorn (5763, from Roon Wildmane in
#   Desolace), and for warriors Cyclonian (1712, from Bath'rah in the Alterac Mountains): its 30
#   Bloodscalp Tusks drop only here; Alterac Mountains & Arathi Highlands (38-39) hands it in.
# Left to later guides: Report to Rog'mar (95141), handed in by Riverglades (40-41), and Cyclonian
#   (1712), handed in by Alterac Mountains & Arathi Highlands (38-39).
#
# The route: the zeppelin to Grom'gol; the road south to Booty Bay for its quests, the hearthstone
# and the flight path; a flight back and the ride north to Nesingwary's camp; a loop around the camp
# (young tigers, young panthers, crocolisks); a loop west (tigers, panthers, the Ruins of Zul'Kunda,
# the raptors and basilisks south of them); a loop east and south (the Venture Co. geologists, the
# Lashtail raptors, the elder tigers); the hearthstone to Booty Bay, a flight to Grom'gol and the
# zeppelin to Orgrimmar, where the next guide starts.

guide Stranglethorn Vale (36-37)
faction horde
levels 36 37
carry 1106 1136 1373 1712 1714 5762 5763
leave 1106 1136 1373 1712 1714 95141
next Dustwallow Marsh (37-38)

map Stranglethorn Vale

# Grom'gol Base Camp --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

goto "Ride the zeppelin from the tower outside Orgrimmar to Grom'gol Base Camp" at 31.5,29.5 r 30
fpath 1387
accept 568
tip Commander Aggro'gosh paces around the middle of the camp.
accept 95141
tip Krom'rosh is in the Riverglades, far to the north-east: keep this one, the Riverglades guide hands it in.
accept 581

# Booty Bay -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

goto "Follow the road south through the jungle to Booty Bay, at the southern tip of Stranglethorn" at 28.1,74.4 r 25
tip Keep to the road: the trolls, ogres and raptors away from it are higher level than you.
accept 201
tip Krazek and Kebok stand on the top floor of the inn; Crank Fizzlebub is on its ground floor.
accept 189 213
accept 605
bind 6807
accept 575
tip Drizzlik has a shop on the upper walkway on the far side of the bay.
fpath 2858
tip Gringer keeps his bats on the balcony at the top of the inn.
fly "Grom'gol, Stranglethorn" npc 2858

# Nesingwary's camp -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

do 201 at 35.7,10.6 icon text "Ride north on the road from Grom'gol to Nesingwary's camp, by the river"
turnin 5762
turnin 5763
accept 583
turnin 583
accept 194
accept 185
accept 190

# Around the camp: young tigers, young panthers, crocolisks -------------------------------------------

do 575 bg
tip The River Crocolisks swim in the river beside the camp and further east; not every one has a good skin.
do 185
tip The Young Stranglethorn Tigers prowl all around the camp.
do 190
tip The Young Panthers stalk the jungle east of the camp.
do 575
turnin 185
accept 186
turnin 190
accept 191

# West: tigers, panthers, the Ruins of Zul'Kunda, raptors and basilisks ------------------------------

do 186 bg at 29.8,10.4
do 191 bg
tip Tigers and panthers share the hills between the camp and the ruins.
accept 97328
tip The Thoroughly Scavenged Supplies are the wreckage of a crashed zeppelin on the hill west of the camp.
do 97328 bg
tip The Stolen Shipments are crates lying around the Ruins of Zul'Kunda.
do 189 bg
do 581 bg
tip Warriors on Cyclonian: collect only Nimboya's 9 tusks here. Players report that handing in Hunt for Yenniku takes every Bloodscalp Tusk you carry, so Bath'rah's 30 come after it, at the end of the guide.
accept 97329
tip Zimmix Sputterspark, a goblin, is locked in a cage in the south of the ruins.
do 97329
tip The key is a rare drop from any of the Bloodscalp trolls in the ruins: it will come while you collect the rest.
do 97328
do 189
do 581
turnin 97329
accept 97331
do 97331 at 26.9,11.4 icon text "Escort Zimmix Sputterspark out of the ruins to the east"
tip Zimmix makes for the east edge of the ruins: stay close and pull the trolls off him.
do 605 bg
do 194
tip The Stranglethorn Raptors hunt in the jungle south of the ruins.
do 605
tip The Crystal Spine Basilisks bask on the rocks south of the ruins, beside the raptors.
do 186 at 29.8,10.4
do 191
turnin 186
accept 187
turnin 191
turnin 194
accept 195

# East and south: the geologists, the Lashtail raptors, the elder tigers ------------------------------

do 213
tip The Venture Co. Geologists work around the goblin camp on the shore of Lake Nazferiti, east of Nesingwary's.
do 187 bg
do 195 at 37.9,19.8
tip The Lashtail Raptors hunt in the jungle south-west of Lake Nazferiti; more roam south toward Grom'gol.
do 568 at 37.9,19.8
do 187
tip The Elder Stranglethorn Tigers keep to the hills south of Nesingwary's camp.
turnin 187
turnin 195

# Booty Bay and Grom'gol ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

hearth npc 6807
turnin 201
turnin 189 213
turnin 605
turnin 575
turnin 97328
tip Wharfmaster Lozgil stands on the docks at the north of the bay.
turnin 97331
fly "Grom'gol, Stranglethorn" npc 2858
turnin 568
turnin 581
do 1712.2 only warrior
tip Warriors only: now gather Bath'rah's 30 Bloodscalp Tusks from the Bloodscalp trolls, the nearest north-west of Grom'gol. Handing in Hunt for Yenniku first keeps them safe.
note "Take the zeppelin from the Grom'gol tower to Orgrimmar: the next guide starts there" at 31.5,29.5
